  "title": "Home, things and where they are",
  "note": "あります is \"there is\" for objects; います is for people and animals. The place takes に: 机の上に本があります \"There is a book on the desk.\" Position words follow の: 机の上 (on), 下 (under), 中 (in). これ, それ, あれ mean this one, that one near you, and that one over there; ここ, そこ, あそこ are the matching places.",
